shots/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env

# per-scene Deck screenshots, regenerated by `--shots`
tests/steam-deck/shots/

# THE AUTHORED SPRITE SHEETS STAY OUT OF GIT. Josh's call, 2026-09-12:
# "keep any SS sheets uncommitted including the kid sheets". They are ~1.5GB
# of source art; what the game loads is the built atlases under
# game/assets/sprites, and tools/prep_sprites.py rebuilds those from a local
# copy of the sheets. The LFS rule in .gitattributes only ever matched the
# top level, so animations/kids/ (208MB) would have gone in as plain blobs.
animations/SS_*.png
animations/kids/SS_*.png
# The enemies' sheets (2026-09-13 on) are the same call: 917MB of them by 09-14,
# in a subfolder neither rule above reaches.
animations/sprites/enemies/animations/SS_*.png

# Local safety copies and reference photographs, far too large for the repo (2.2 GB and
# 270 MB on 2026-11-03). Text in the review folders is still tracked.
docs/rollbacks/
docs/ingame-narrative-2026-10-27/**/*.jpg
docs/ingame-narrative-2026-10-27/**/*.png
docs/enemy-roster-2026-10-26/**/*.jpg
docs/enemy-roster-2026-10-26/**/*.png
docs/enemy-sprites-2026-10-27/**/*.jpg
docs/enemy-sprites-2026-10-27/**/*.png
# Source paintings: what the game hangs is built from these and lives under game/assets/ui.
game/assets/Portrait Paintings/
# Scratch images and PDFs from helper scripts; the scripts themselves are tracked.
tmp/*.png
tmp/pdfs/
tmp/__pycache__/
docs/enemy-sprites-2026-10-27/**/*.zip
docs/enemy-roster-2026-10-26/**/*.webp
